Subject: About interpretation of K and loadings in PACA
Message-ID: <bfysNoDWn-Y.6hrp20IpCwAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/bfysNoDWn-Y/m/6hrp20IpCwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello
everybody, I am running a PACA on log-shape ratios of linear skull
measurements. The data has a strong phylogenetic signal (Kmult:
1.6266, P-value: 0.001) with a considerable effect size 5.1437.
Moreover, the K on the first component is quite large 2.603, and then
drops down to 0.48 in K2. So, I assume that the signal was
concentrated in some variables of the original data (similar to
empiric example 1 in Collyer and Admas 2020). In the context of PACA,
is valid to analyze the loadings in the first component in search of
the variable who most contribute to component 1, or in this case, in
the phylogenetic signal?

Kind
regards,

Ale

From uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com  Wed Apr 14 13:17:40 2021
